+# Fälligkeitsdatum für Todos — Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Give todos an optional due date (`due`, `YYYY-MM-DD`), expose a computed `overdue` flag in every API todo response, support `GET /todos?overdue=true`, and show the date, an overdue marker, and a "nur überfällige" toggle on the list page.
+
+**Architecture:** `src/store.mjs` validates `due` and attaches a computed `overdue` (against the UTC calendar date) to every returned todo; `src/app.mjs` adds the `?overdue=` query filter on `GET /todos`; `public/index.html` renders due date, overdue marker, and the toggle client-side from the existing `GET /todos` payload.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Node 24 builtins only (`node:http`, `node:test`) — zero dependencies. Playwright MCP tools for the end-to-end check in Task 4.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-01-faelligkeitsdatum-design.md` (approved; posted as "Approved Spec" on ticket #1)
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Zero dependencies — Node builtins only.
+- Validation errors are `ValidationError` from `src/store.mjs` and map to HTTP 400.
+- TDD: write a failing test in `test/` first (AGENTS.md).
+- Every UI element tests rely on carries a `data-testid` (existing: `todo-list`, `todo-item`, `todo-title`; new: `todo-due`, `todo-overdue`, `overdue-only-toggle`).
+- Page is German (`lang="de"`); due dates render as `TT.MM.JJJJ`.
+- "Today" is the UTC calendar date (`new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10)`); a todo due today is not yet overdue; a done todo is never overdue.
+- Work on branch `1_faelligkeitsdatum`; one commit per task.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+1. Strings that pass a naive regex but are not real calendar dates (`2026-02-30`, `2027-02-29`, `2026-1-1`) must return 400 — pinned by Task 1 tests.
+2. Leap day `2028-02-29` is valid — pinned by Task 1.
+3. Boundary semantics: due *today* (UTC) is not overdue, due yesterday is; done todo with past due is not overdue — pinned by Task 1 with an injected fixed clock (also proves UTC, not server-local, "today").
+4. `GET /todos?overdue=banana` must 400, not be silently ignored — pinned by Task 2.
+5. `PATCH {due: null}` removes the date and clears `overdue`; the toggle lists only overdue items — pinned by Tasks 1/3 and verified e2e in Task 4.
+
+---
+
+### Task 1: Store — optional `due`, validation, computed `overdue`
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `src/store.mjs`
+- Modify: `test/app.test.mjs`
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: nothing new.
+- Produces: `createStore(now = () => new Date())` — optional injected clock (app keeps calling `createStore()`); `add({ title, due })` accepts `due` (`YYYY-MM-DD` string or `null`, default `null`) and returns `{ id, title, done, due, overdue }`; `update(id, patch)` accepts `due` (string or `null`; `null` removes it); `list()` and `get(id)` return todos including `overdue`; invalid `due` throws `ValidationError('due must be a YYYY-MM-DD date')`. `overdue` is computed at read time: `due !== null && !done && due < todayUTC`, where `todayUTC = now().toISOString().slice(0, 10)`.
